{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1451259-trinity-core-super-science-crafting-table-enhancements-edges","id":1451259,"title":"(Trinity Core) Super Science Crafting Table Enhancements & Edges","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-06-07T14:52:13-07:00","id":1451259,"title":"(Trinity Core) Super Science Crafting Table Enhancements & Edges","content":"How do you determine the number of Edges / Enhancement a Device can have? I get that a Rank 1 Device can have 2 Enhance, and 1 Edge, whilst its 3 Enhance and 3 dots for Rank 2.<br /> <br /> But Rank 3+ has me stumped. You can have either max Enhance or max Edge, but how much of the other can you have? <br /> <br /> I've tried to work backwards from the examples, but drawn a blank.<br /> <br /> (for reference, I'm referring to the table at the bottom of p91 of the Trinity Core (and the equivalents for Aberrant on p234 and 235)).<br /> <br /> Apologies if I'm being thick.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4972-hurum","name":"hurum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-08T05:16:26-07:00","id":1451300,"title":"","content":"RAW, just one less than max. However, I really like using the optional choice of adding the two together and not letting them get above the max number of enhancements.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-09T02:09:52-07:00","id":1451424,"title":"","content":"Thanks Florin. I was obviously overthinking things<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4972-hurum","name":"hurum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-09T05:40:03-07:00","id":1451433,"title":"","content":"I had to have it pointed out to me too. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-10T07:47:36-07:00","id":1451541,"title":"","content":"Not really responsive to the original question, but here's a related thought I've gone back and forth on: Depending on the era different types of equipment receive extra tags to indicate the general improvement of technology. I think the way this interacts with the superscience rules is a bit odd. In core, and even Aberrant everything works find, but once you get to the Aeon era regular tech gets so many more tags than superscience that the superscience stuff built with the system from the core almost always seems lack luster to me. The special rules for bioware in the aexpansion work fine, but if I want a talent to invent a super cool piece of armor or weapon that armor or weapon often has half the tags a regular thing would have.<br /> <br /> TLDR; what do you think about adding the extra tags for item type based on era for superscience stuff? Sometimes I like the idea, other times I think it ends up a little OP.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6-slagheap","name":"Slagheap","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"188"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-02T10:03:47-07:00","id":1456013,"title":"","content":"hey <span style=\"color:#0066ff\">Florin</span>, could you please elaborate? I <b><i>still </i></b>didn't get it (maybe with the <i>Freeze Ray</i> at Trinity Core p.91 could be a good example). \ud83d\ude2d.<br /> <br /> Also, can you please illustrate with the <b>Cyber Suit </b>Q-Tech? (in the Q-Tech table at Aberrant p.243).<br /> <br /> FYI: [<i><b>Cyber Suit</b></i>: <b>Rank </b>7, <b>Enhancement </b>4, <b>Edges</b>: {Mega-Might 3 (Intrinsic), Mega-Dexterity1 (Intrinsic), Digital Scan, Spectrum Vision (Modular), Ultraperipheral Perception (Modular)}, <b>Quantum Powers</b>: {Flight (Modular), Quantum Attack 4 (Aggravated, Beam, Ranged:Medium) } , <b>Tags</b>: {Modular: Quantum Power 2, Mega-Attribute 2, Mega-Edge 3}, <b>Flaws</b>: {Kickstart Required 2} ].<br /> <br /> The specific mega-crafting info for Rank 7 is (Aberrant p.235) is: &quot;Rank 7 Q-Tech = Quantum Minimum 5, Maximum Enhancement 9, Maximum Edge Dots = <i>Up to 30 dots (all types) but no more than 12 dots in Quantum Abilities</i>, Maximum Tag Bonuses 8.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1001-timecrafter","name":"Timecrafter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1001_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-02T10:21:40-07:00","id":1456015,"title":"","content":"For a Rank 7 item, you have a choice of maximums. You can either have the maximum enhancement of 9 and a max of 29 dots of edges. OR you can have 30 dots of edges and 8 enhancements. That's RAW. They also have an optional rule where you cannot have a total of enhancements + dots of edges greater than the max enhancement number, which for Rank 7 is 9. That optional rule is really going to hamper mega-crafting compared to the standard rules.<br /> <br /> The Cyber-Suit is actually under all the RAW maximums.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-02T12:22:09-07:00","id":1456024,"title":"","content":"wow... 1) so you're telling me that the Math doesn't &quot;add up&quot; simply because the book examples <i>could </i>use a lot of points, but <i>chose </i>to not use them? (just because &quot;nah, I won't use all my edge points&quot;) =S I mean, if the player wanted, they could be stronger than listed??? =S<br /> <br /> 2) That's the case with both Core and Aberrant super-Science? o.O<br /> <br /> that's really really weird; everything in this system normally adds up mathematically in a very restrict way o.O","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1001-timecrafter","name":"Timecrafter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1001_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-05T11:18:24-07:00","id":1456193,"title":"","content":"Hello, another dumb guy here. I still don't get how it works. Either it's poorly explained or I'm missing something. So, when you pick a rank you get all the enhancements, edges, and tags, but the only difference is which one gets the maximum while the other two go one below, is that correct?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-06T06:08:33-07:00","id":1456228,"title":"","content":"It is a bit confusing and needs a bit of clarification for instance if a nova is in aeon time period how would mega intelligence crafting work would you just take the time periods tech level as the base from which the nova can craft from so their tech can still be considered more advanced?<br /> <br /> Ps sorry if I haven\u2019t worded this well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26058-aeonstorm","name":"Aeonstorm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-06T08:50:16-07:00","id":1456241,"title":"","content":"Yeah, super-science is always based off of the baseline assumption of the setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-09T06:26:29-07:00","id":1456423,"title":"","content":"Any patient souls out there willing to explain how the process works step by step for this dummy, pretty please? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}